 "findings": [
  "Tool CPU-s is flat across concurrency (dump 4.0-4.9 CPU-s, restore 7.4-8.0 CPU-s per 1M docs): concurrency adds no client-side overhead; the curves are engine-bound.",
  "PIT scales to ~4.2-4.4x at 16 slices on 1 or 4 shards (~500k docs/s); scroll only scales up to slices = shards (4 on 4: 3.19x, ~410k docs/s).",
  "Scroll sliced past the shard count is a trap: on the 1-shard index every --slices value from 2 to 16 is slower than unsliced (0.63-0.81x) and costs 5-15x the server CPU; on 4 shards, 8-16 slices fall back to ~1.7x. This matches the README guidance; a warning when --slices exceeds the primary shard count with scroll could be considered (no code change).",
